FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/lsp.rs:1690-1708 (insert at src/lsp.rs:663) — `declare_replacing_binding` writes the replacing variable only into the runtime frame (`scopes[scope_position]`) and never updates the current block scope, so a `set` that shadows a function/object/module declared in the *same* branch body leaves the block's old entry in place. Traced: `if yes then / to f() end / set f to 1 / say f / end` — `to f` lands in the branch scope (declare_function_binding, src/lsp.rs:632), the `set` sees it as non-reusable and inserts the variable into the program scope, then the lookup at src/lsp.rs:1833-1850 hits the branch's stale function entry first and answers the function. The added test only covers a top-level function shadowed from a branch, so this order is untested. Fix: when the runtime frame is not the current scope, also overwrite/remove the name in `scopes.last_mut()`; add `edge_set_shadows_a_function_declared_in_the_same_branch`.
2. [MAJOR] phases/phase-075/REPORT.md:273 — the gate table claims `cargo test --all-targets` reported 2843 passed, but the committed report pinned 2832 and the same uncommitted table lists exactly 8 new tests (five in `+237`, three in `+371`), so 2832 + 8 = 2840, not 2843. Either three added tests are unlisted or the count is stale/fabricated, which is exactly the gate-honesty value `verify.sh` is supposed to read. Fix: re-run and record the real count, or name the three missing tests.
3. [MINOR] src/lsp.rs:1082-1089 — `scope_function_binding` accepts any function binding with `id > first` in the same scope without checking it is declared before the use token, so `to f() end / set f to 1 / say f() / to f() end` resolves the middle call to the *later* function even though the slot holds the variable there. No test covers the set-before-later-function-with-a-call-between order; decide whether forward resolution is intended and either bound the search by source position or document the hoisting rule and pin it with a test. Not verified by execution.

